  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal &amp; Delta Management visitors programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A coherent and integrated approach is lacking in addressing the management challenges of coastal and delta areas in Ghana. Various government agencies are responsible for sectoral aspects only. Institutional mechanisms to coordinate planning and management are lacking. Emergencies like flooding and erosion are dealt with in an ad-hoc manner. Likewise, private investments in the area are hampered by this lack of institutional coordination.A visitors&apos; programme for (government) stakeholders about delta and coastal management is organised with the following aims: &#x2022;	Putting Ghana on the agenda in the Netherlands as a Delta country to deepen the links and contacts for possible cooperation and commercial interests;&#x2022;	Taking the first steps toward an institutional framework and integrated approach for coastal and delta management in Ghana by getting to a common understanding regarding Delta challenges in Ghana and insight into relevant best practices in the Netherlands and worldwide.</narrative>
  </description>
